[GRC1863] Error: parent reference used during reborrow
   ╭─[ <repo>/compiler/tests/cases/parent-reference-during-reborrow.gr:5:23 ]
   │
 4 │     let child: &mut i32 = &mut *parent;
   │                           ──────┬─────  
   │                                 ╰─────── this reborrow remains live through its final use
 5 │     let copied: i32 = *parent;
   │                       ───┬───  
   │                          ╰───── `parent` is used while its child reborrow is live
   │ 
   │ Help: use the child reference or end its final use before reusing the parent
   │ 
   │ Note: a unique reborrow temporarily suspends access through its parent reference
